flowchart TB
  accTitle: DorkOS systems and deployment boundaries
  accDescr: The client reaches the local execution server. The space server is a second entry and image target of the same server package, with its own Postgres and sign-in. Cloud space management uses a separate public server API contract; rollout is independent of local implementation. Marketplace discovery and installation use the same package sources. Hub and agent-computer roles of the same program are omitted here; see the roles view.
  client["DorkOS client · React<br/>Browser / phone web app / desktop"]
  server["DorkOS server · Hono · role: computer<br/>Projects · Sessions · Rooms · Tasks · Heartbeats<br/>Extensions · Audit · Relay · Mesh<br/>Local SQLite + files"]
  runtime["Local AgentRuntime implementations<br/>Claude Code · Codex app-server · OpenCode sidecar · Doe<br/>computer-local VM (experiment, off)<br/>Runtime-specific history"]
  cloud["Optional DorkOS Cloud<br/>Hosted accounts + service management"]
  community["Space server · same package, own entry + image<br/>One or many spaces · agents as members<br/>Server sign-in · tenant memberships<br/>Own PostgreSQL + blob storage"]
  communityUI["Space website · React<br/>apps/client/src/space"]
  sources["Marketplace sources<br/>Registries + package repositories"]
  site["DorkOS website · Next.js<br/>Docs + marketplace discovery"]
  client <-->|"HTTP commands / WebSocket events<br/>Space SSE"| server
  server -->|"SDK calls / local sidecar / in-process engine"| runtime
  server -->|"Optional HTTPS<br/>Link, heartbeat, managed services, credits"| cloud
  server <-->|"Approved participation · pairing<br/>Qualified HTTP + SSE · availability report"| community
  cloud -.->|"Space-management contract · availability-dependent<br/>HTTPS server API; separate from participation"| community
  communityUI <-->|"HTTP commands / SSE events"| community
  server -->|"Fetch: HTTPS / Git / npm"| sources
  site -->|"HTTPS metadata + READMEs"| sources
